{"acceptance_length": 5.467532467532467, "acceptance_lengths": [3, 4, 1, 5, 1, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 1, 2, 8, 8, 1, 7, 1, 5, 4, 2, 6, 2, 1, 1, 6, 8, 4, 1, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 1, 3, 5, 1, 4, 8, 8, 7, 8, 8, 6, 8, 8, 4, 8, 8, 8, 6, 8, 8, 8, 6, 4, 5, 2, 6, 5, 1, 6, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 7, 8, 8, 8, 3, 1, 1, 4, 8, 3], "accepted_draft_lengths": [2, 3, 0, 4, 0, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 0, 1, 7, 7, 0, 6, 0, 4, 3, 1, 5, 1, 0, 0, 5, 7, 3, 0, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 0, 2, 4, 0, 3, 7, 7, 6, 7, 7, 5, 7, 7, 3, 7, 7, 7, 5, 7, 7, 7, 5, 3, 4, 1, 5, 4, 0, 5, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 6, 7, 7, 7, 2, 0, 0, 3, 7, 3], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 31666454528, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 31666449408, "benchmark": "math500", "completion": "We are given:\n\n- A **cylindrical beaker** with:\n  - Height = 8 cm\n  - Radius = 3 cm\n- A **spherical tank** with:\n  - Radius = 6 cm\n\nWe are to find **how many beakers of water** are needed to **fill the spherical tank**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Find the volume of the **spherical tank**\n\nThe formula for the volume of a sphere is:\n\n$$\nV_{\\text{sphere}} = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi r^3\n$$\n\nGiven $ r = 6 $ cm:\n\n$$\nV_{\\text{sphere}} = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi (6)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi (216) = 288\\pi \\text{ cm}^3\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Find the volume of the **cylindrical beaker**\n\nThe formula for the volume of a cylinder is:\n\n$$\nV_{\\text{cylinder}} = \\pi r^2 h\n$$\n\nGiven $ r = 3 $ cm, $ h = 8 $ cm:\n\n$$\nV_{\\text{cylinder}} = \\pi (3)^2 (8) = \\pi (9)(8) = 72\\pi \\text{ cm}^3\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Find how many beakers are needed to fill the tank\n\nWe divide the volume of the sphere by the volume of one beaker:\n\n$$\n\\text{Number of beakers} = \\frac{V_{\\text{sphere}}}{V_{\\text{cylinder}}} = \\frac{288\\pi}{72\\pi} = \\frac{288}{72} = 4\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{4}\n$$\n\nIt will take **4 beakers** of water to fill the spherical tank.", "decode_seconds": 5.122348630800843, "draft_calls": 77, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 66, "mapper